    "summary": "Razor‑sharp Garcia leads, stellar High Time & Other One → Cosmic Charlie",
    "blurb": "The set delivers razor‑sharp Jerry leads on High Time and The Other One, highlighted by a powerful Other One → Cosmic Charlie sequence despite a brief edit. Tom Constanten’s keyboards add color on China Cat Sunflower while the band moves from energetic early numbers into mellow grooves. The soundboard capture is clear and showcases one of 1970’s underrated performances.",
    "review": "On January 30, 1970 at New Orleans’ Warehouse, the Dead rolled out a tight, high‑energy set that still feels fresh decades later. Garcia’s lead work is razor‑sharp throughout – his tone on High Time is flawless and he rides The Other One with fierce intensity, leading into an exhilarating Other One → Cosmic Charlie stretch (the only blemish being a short edit). Tom Constanten, making his final appearance with the group, provides audible but occasionally muddy keys that truly shine on China Cat Sunflower and lend subtle texture to High Time. The rhythm section stays solid as the band slides from raucous openers like Casey Jones into smoother territory with Black Peter, Easy Wind, and Cumberland Blues, delivering a well‑balanced flow that rewards repeated listening.",
